# Elemental Skin & Body: Cursor Rules
# Med Spa | Elkhorn, WI | Astro Framework

## Framework
- Astro only; `output: 'static'` unless SSR is explicitly required.
- Content Collections for blog/multi-page editorial content when added.
- Prefer `.astro` components; minimal client JS.
- Interactivity: Astro islands with React.
- TypeScript preferred.
- Do not use `<form>` HTML elements; use React islands with `onClick`/`onChange` for user-driven submission (see `src/islands/ContactForm.tsx`).

## Structure
See `src/pages`, `src/layouts`, `src/components`, `src/config/siteConfig.ts`, `src/styles/global.css`.

## SEO (every page)
- Unique `<title>`: `Service Name | Elemental Skin & Body, Elkhorn, WI` (pattern).
- Unique meta description (150–160 chars, primary keyword).
- Canonical via absolute URL from `siteConfig.url` + `Astro.url.pathname`.
- Open Graph: `og:title`, `og:description`, `og:image`, `og:type`, `og:url`.
- `@astrojs/sitemap` enabled in `astro.config.mjs`.
- `public/robots.txt` references sitemap URL (update domain with `siteConfig.url`).
- JSON-LD: homepage `MedicalBusiness` + `LocalBusiness`; services `MedicalProcedure` + `BreadcrumbList`; about `MedicalOrganization`.
- Semantic headings: one `h1` per page.
- Internal links: each service page links to 2+ related services via `getRelatedServices`.

## URL structure
Follow routes in `siteConfig.nav.services` and `src/data/serviceRegistry.ts`; do not change slugs without redirects.

## Security
- Never commit API keys; use `// TODO: add to .env` for secrets.
- `bookingUrl` only from `siteConfig.bookingUrl`.
- External anchors: `rel="noopener noreferrer"`.
- Server-side validation for contact submissions in `netlify/functions/contact.ts`.
- Security headers in `netlify.toml` (CSP allows Google Fonts, Maps embed, GA, Vagaro as configured).

## Brand
Use CSS variables in `src/styles/global.css`; avoid hardcoded hex in components.

## Booking
Vagaro opens in a new tab via `bookingUrl`; no iframe embed.
